#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# generating_function

#% text
# `generating_function(f, n, z)` gives the sum of `f z^n` over `n >= 0` in closed form.

#% text
# `generating_function(f, [n, m], [x, y])` gives the generating function in several variables.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `generate_conditions: true` attaches the convergence region `abs(z) < 1/r` of the ratio test, r the limit of `abs(f(n + 1)/f(n))`.

#% item
# The function is linear; lists, equations and rules thread.

#% item
# An unknown sequence `g(n + s)` is expressed through `generating_function(g(n), n, z)` by the shift rules; `b^n g(n)` is that function at `b z`.

#% item
# Known terms are summed by `sum`: polynomials times powers, hypergeometric series (with Bessel and exponential closed forms), rational functions.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
generating_function(a^n, n, z)
#% output
#= (1 - a*z)^-1

#% cell
generating_function(n*(n + 1)*(-1/2)^n, n, z)
#% output
#= -8*z/(2 + z)^3

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
generating_function(1/factorial(n)^2, n, x)
#% output
#= bessel_i(0, 2*x^(1/2))

#% cell
generating_function(1/(factorial(n + 1)*factorial(m)), [n, m], [x, y])
#% output
#= (-1 + exp(x))*exp(y)/x

#% text
# Shift rules:

#% cell
generating_function([f(n + 1), f(n - 1)], n, z)
#% output
#= [generating_function(f(n), n, z)/z - f(0)/z, f(-1) + z*generating_function(f(n), n, z)]

